	abstract = {The solubilities of Fe₂O₃, NiO, and NiFe₂O₄ have been measured in NaF-AlF₃-CaF₂-Al₂O₃ melts as a function of temperature and melt composition.  The solubilities of Fe₂O₃ and NiO for melts containing 1.5 to 6.5 wt\% Al₂O₃ and for bath ratios ranging from 0.5 to 1.5 are represented by the relationships
log wt\% Fe = 4.71 - 7080/T,
and
log wt\% Ni = 6.27 - 9740/T,
respectively.  The solubilities of both Fe₂O₃ and NiO increased with decreasing concentrations of Al₂O₃ in the melt, particularly at {\textless}1 wt\% Al₂O₃.  The solubility of Fe₂O₃ decreased moderately with decreasing bath ratio (wt NaF/wth AlF₃), while no change occurred for NiO.  The solubility of NiFe₂O₄ was less than the solubilities of Fe₂O₃ and NiO, and there was good agreement between the free energy of formation of NiFe₂O₄ calculated from the measured solubilities of Fe₂O₃, NiO, and NiFe₂O₄ and the free energy of formation reported in the literature.},
	language = {en},
