	title = {Direct {Carbon} {Fuel} {Cell} {With} {Novel} {Liquid} {Metal} {Alloy} {Anode}},
	abstract = {Direct Carbon Fuel Cells (DCFCs) are electrochemical devices that utilize solid carbon fuel dissolved in a liquid metal alloy to convert the energy from a chemical reaction into electricity. This produces a nearly pure CO2 off-gas which can be captured for sequestration, making DCFCs a greener source of energy than other carbon-based techniques. This paper focuses on the development of DCFC technology, improves on the cathode-electrolyte-support ceramic manufacturing process, and discusses stirring and reverse voltage to address mass transfer resistance and increase fuel cell consistency. Optimizations include improvements to the de-gassing process and the smoothing of support structure molds which reduced cracking and formation of imperfections on the structure surface.},
