	abstract = {Magnesium-tin-antimony (Mg–Sn–Sb) system is a promising system for developing high-creep resistance mag­ nesium alloy and the alloy-type anode of magnesium recharge battery. Herein, the thermodynamic assessment of Mg–Sn–Sb ternary system was carried out using the CALculaiton of PHAse Diagram (CALPHAD) approach based on available literature data. The liquid phase was described via the associated model with associates Mg3Sb2 and Mg2Sn, and the compounds were described using the sublattice model. The consistency of the calculated phase equilibria relations and thermochemical properties with the available experimental data of Mg–Sn–Sb ternary system is presented. The thermodynamic descriptions of Mg–Sb, Sn–Sb binary systems and Mg–Sn–Sb ternary system assessed in this work provide a thermodynamic basis for the alloy design of magnesium alloy.},
