	doi = {10.1134/S0036023611100275},
	abstract = {Isothermal anneals (at 873 K) and powder X ray diffraction were used to study isothermal sections of phase diagrams of the NdF3–Nd2O3–MF2 (M = Ba, Sr) systems. In studying the NdF3–Nd2O3–BaF2 sys tem, classical solid phase synthesis was supplemented with mechanochemical activation of feedstock mix tures or BaF2 activated with gaseous hydrogen fluoride was used. In both systems, a solid solution with the fluorite structure based on MF2 and NdOF phases, a solid solution with the tysonite structure based on NdF3, and an ordered fluorite related phase Ba4Nd3F17 were found. The NdOF based solid solutions were shown to have polymorphism: βtrig αcub at ≈800 K; a new trigonal phase of these solid solutions has been discove red. The effect of a dimensional factor (RBa2+ {\textgreater} RSr2+ ) on phase formation and unit cell parameters of the solid solutions was traced.},
