	abstract = {The thermodynamic properties of Fe-C-Sn liquid solutions have been studied by using the solubility method in the temperature range 1300-1500°C and by using the iso-tin-activity with a silver bath at 1500°C. The temperature dependences of interaction coefficients between Sn and C in C saturated liquid Fe and between Sn and C in liquid Fe are derived. The first and second order interaction coefficients between Sn and C in liquid Fe at 1550 °C are determined.
